{"type":"text","timestamp":1790448752134,"sessionID":"ses_f20f34870ffeStCDxx4M43WojK","part":{"id":"prt_0df0fd5f5001LzeB0bpL1Hbnwo","messageID":"msg_0df0fae450016WmWVf6MxEhkke","sessionID":"ses_f20f34870ffeStCDxx4M43WojK","type":"text","text":"Rendered scene looks wrong — the camera isn't seeing the spheres. The issue is likely the camera's rotation is making it look away from the spheres. Let me check: spheres are at z ∈ [3.2, 4.5], camera at z=0.2, so camera must look toward +z. Default Camera3D looks toward -z, so yaw=π should flip it. But the image shows ground/water only. Let me debug with a script that prints the camera's view and whether spheres are visible.","time":{"start":1790448752117,"end":1790448752121},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"resp_628ca0aefbf54e1db6a7649fe3e72179_msg"}}}}
